per BF16 weight, so 3.37 bits per weight for the exponent and escapes on top of the 8 kept bits of
sign and mantissa.

### lib/hx-cm, stack growth (Finding 3) tested further

gcc 13 and clang 18 at -O2 both nest frames per byte (484 MB and 721 MB of stack after 3 s on a 2 MB
input). The cycle is a chain of functions of 15 to 24 arguments; on x86-64 a sibling call is made only
when the callee's stack arguments fit in the caller's, and they do not along this chain. Patching the
emitted C cannot fix it short of rewriting the loop; the fix is in the emitter (a self tail call
emitted as a loop, or calls through a trampoline) or in hx-cm (loop state in at most 6 words for
x86-64, 8 for ARM64, as its header intends). Whole `dickens` (10 MB) needs about 11 GB at the measured
rate and was not run on this 8 GB machine.

